== F. Proposition A: stationary sticky valuation chains ==
   kernel P(v -> w) = p [w = v] + (1-p) 2^(-w): for any law pi, (pi P)(w) = p pi(w) + (1-p) 2^(-w), so pi P = pi iff pi = geometric(1/2):
   the geometric law is the UNIQUE stationary law; the chain is irreducible, aperiodic (P(v->v) >= p > 0) and regenerates with
   probability 1-p per step, hence ergodic; E[v] = 2 < infinity: the ergodic theorem applies and the a.s. slope is log2 3 - 2 = -0.4150
   simulated chain p = 0.9, 2000000 steps (own seed): empirical marginal P(v=k) vs 2^-k: k=1: 0.4979/0.5000, k=2: 0.2527/0.2500, k=3: 0.1247/0.1250, k=4: 0.0628/0.0625, k=5: 0.0310/0.0312, k=6: 0.0151/0.0156, k=7: 0.0079/0.0078, k=8: 0.0039/0.0039
      P(v_(l+1) = 1 | v_l = 1) = 0.9498 (exact (1+p)/2 = 0.95); mean v = 2.0007; slope -0.4157
   200 paths x 4000 steps per persistence (own seed):
      p=0.00: mean slope -0.4192 (s.e. 0.0015; theory s.e. 0.0016); mean max height 1.0; paths above start at the end: 0/200
      p=0.50: mean slope -0.4132 (s.e. 0.0027; theory s.e. 0.0027); mean max height 3.1; paths above start at the end: 0/200
      p=0.90: mean slope -0.4048 (s.e. 0.0074; theory s.e. 0.0069); mean max height 17.5; paths above start at the end: 0/200
      p=0.99: mean slope -0.4169 (s.e. 0.0217; theory s.e. 0.0223); mean max height 201.1; paths above start at the end: 12/200
