== G. Proposition B: escape products ==
   escape 3/sqrt(N) from N0 = 2^20, r = 2^0.3: sum p_k over 20000 steps = 0.02967, exact P(never leave in 20000 steps) = 0.9707; infinite product = 0.9707; 1 - sum = 0.9703
   escape 0.6/ln N: sum over 20000 steps = 16.49 (harmonic, diverges like (0.6/(0.3 ln 2)) ln k), exact P(never leave in 20000 steps) = 6.48e-08
   simulation (2000 trials, own seed): never leaving in 20000 steps with escape 3/sqrt(N): 0.965
   caveat on the statement: 'positive iff sum < infinity' needs p(N_0 r^k) < 1 for all k (else the product is 0 with a finite sum); 'over renewed visits, infinitely often' presupposes infinitely many visits (each visit ends a.s., so if the state is visited infinitely often it is left infinitely often)
[  36.0s]

== H. Tenth note, Proposition 1 (Apery form) and Proposition 3 (free cofactor), Proposition 3(d) (LTE) ==
   odd n < 4000, all 54813 orbit steps: v2(3^j n + S_(j-1)) = D_j = v_0 + ... + v_(j-1) (cumulative) and 3^j n + S_(j-1) = 2^(D_j) m_j: True
   with the PER-STEP valuation v_(j-1) in place of D_j the identity fails on 52814 of the 54813 steps (e.g. n = 7, j = 2: A_2 = 63 + 3 + 2 = 68 = 2^2 * 17, v2 = 2 = 1 + 1)
   so Proposition 1 is correct with d_j = the cumulative 2-adic exponent of the Apery form (the first note's convention, and the script's 'd += v'); the tenth note does not say so
